course: dictionary
lesson: 4443
title: Handstand: a word from PE
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A handstand is a noun, so it names a thing you can do. Context helps you find its meaning. «Do a handstand» and «hold a handstand» tell you it is a position you can make and keep still.
explain: «Cartwheels and handstands at home are practised on grass or a mat, away from furniture.» Practised tells you handstands are a skill you get better at with practice. Away from furniture tells you they need space, so you do not hit a table or chair.
explain: Other words near handstand also give clues. Cartwheel, forward roll and headstand are all gymnastics moves, so handstand is one too. Ask yourself what would fit, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A handstand is a position where you balance upside down on your hands.
fact: In a handstand your legs are straight up in the air.
fact: In PE and gymnastics, the handstand is a basic skill.
fact: Children often practise handstands on a mat, with someone nearby spotting them.
fact: «Spotted skunks even do a handstand» as a warning to an attacker, before they spray.
exercise: «Cartwheels and handstands at home are practised on grass or a mat, away from furniture.» Where should you practise handstands at home? | Next to a glass table | *On grass or a mat, away from furniture | On a wobbly chair | On the top of a bookshelf
exercise: What is a handstand? | Jumping as high as you can | Rolling over and over on the grass | Sitting on the floor with your legs crossed | *Balancing upside down on your hands, legs straight up in the air
exercise: «Spotted skunks even do a handstand» before they spray. Why would a skunk do a handstand? | To climb up a tree | *To warn an attacker before it sprays | To show off to its friends | To get a drink of water
test: Which word is a related gymnastics move to handstand? | Breakfast | Whisper | *Headstand | Furniture
test: Why do children practise handstands with someone spotting them? | To make their legs longer | To make the mat dirty | *To help keep them safe while they learn | Because a handstand is a spelling test
exam: Which sentence uses handstand correctly? | Mia is very handstand today. | Mia handstand to the shop yesterday. | *Mia can hold a handstand against the wall. | Mia handstands the ball across the room.
